-*   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources. The output binary grid requires $O(N)$ bits or bytes, and the input SDF requires $O(N)$ floats [G].
-*   **Strengths:** Not given in the sources. Extremely fast conversion; simple implementation; produces clean binary masks suitable for boolean operations or marching cubes [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Not given in the sources. Loses all distance information; sensitive to grid alignment (voxel center sampling); may produce topological errors (holes, bridges) if the grid resolution is too low relative to the object's curvature [G].
-*   **When to use:** Not given in the sources. When a binary mask is sufficient for rendering (e.g., ray marching with early termination) or when preparing data for boolean CSG operations [G].
